x86_64-linux  The C1 and D1 forms, and nothing else: every C2 and D2 name agrees with clang letter for letter. clang emits only the base-object C2 and D2 forms of a constructor and destructor defined *inside* their class on this target, where cxx1 emits the complete-object forms beside them - the fact polymorphic-class-template.nonames and move-constructor.nonames already record. The constructors here cannot move out of line: the case is about the in-class spelling `V<N>(`, and an out-of-line constructor of a class template is refused. x86_64-windows and arm64-darwin agree name for name.
